        {
          "day": 1,
          "number": 5,
          "problem": "Consider a nonempty family $\\mathcal F$ of permutations of an $n$-element set, with $2\\le k\\le n$. Assume each $\\sigma\\in\\mathcal F$ has positions $i_1<\\cdots<i_k$ such that interchanging entries at $i_j$ and $i_{j+1}$ produces another member of $\\mathcal F$, for every $j=1,\\ldots,k-1$. Prove $|\\mathcal F|\\ge k!$.",
